    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d520">

                <pb facs="0553" n="473" sameAs="frus:frus1930v01/pg473"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.51632 National City Bank/45: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Morgan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-07-11T10:00:00-03:00">July 11, 1930—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 10:15 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>41. Embassy’s 40, July 2, 2 p.m.<anchor n="31" xml:id="d520-f1"/> The President
                    informed me yesterday afternoon that he had instructed the Minister of Finance
                    to issue an administrative order canceling in its entirety the fine levied by
                    the Inspector of Banks on National City Bank.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Morgan</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
